cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use lexsync, please cite both the software and the accompanying article.'
title: 'lexsync: multidimensional lexical optimisation and hardware-timed experiment generation'
abstract: >-
  lexsync is a cross-platform, dual-language (R and Python) toolkit that unifies
  many-language lexical-corpus access, parallel multidimensional stimulus
  matching, counterbalancing and the automated generation of hardware-timed
  PsychoPy and OpenSesame experiment scripts for EEG/ERP research.
type: software
